{# Variants
   The variant tells how important the message is. Use success, info, warning
   and danger for most messages; the other variants are less common. #}
<twig:ea:Alert variant="success">The invoice INV-2026-0042 was sent to the customer.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="info">Prices include VAT for customers in the European Union.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="warning">This product has only 3 units left in stock.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="danger">The payment was rejected by the bank.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="primary">New orders are now synced every 5 minutes.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="secondary">This customer was imported from the old system.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="light">Last updated 2 hours ago.</twig:ea:Alert>
<twig:ea:Alert variant="dark">Maintenance mode is enabled.</twig:ea:Alert>
